WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.983 --> 00:00:01.619
- [Voiceover] Here are some things

00:00:01.619 --> 00:00:04.132
men may not know about their clothes.

00:00:04.132 --> 00:00:06.288
The Boat Shoe was invented by Paul Sperry.

00:00:06.288 --> 00:00:09.025
The sole of the shoe was
modeled after his dogs paw;

00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:10.898
the dog has no memory of this.

00:00:10.898 --> 00:00:13.795
Men who wear Bow Ties are
seen as older, smarter,

00:00:13.795 --> 00:00:16.473
brainier, and Republicaner.

00:00:16.473 --> 00:00:19.769
This button was inspired by
polo players who'd put buttons

00:00:19.769 --> 00:00:23.391
on their collars to keep them
from flying up while playing.

00:00:23.391 --> 00:00:25.204
While we're on the subject of polo,

00:00:25.204 --> 00:00:28.511
Polo Shirts were created
for tennis, not polo.

00:00:28.511 --> 00:00:30.333
But, back to buttons on collars.

00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:32.096
Shirts with button-down collars

00:00:32.096 --> 00:00:33.963
are called button-down shirts,

00:00:33.963 --> 00:00:35.664
but shirts that button in the front

00:00:35.664 --> 00:00:37.478
and don't have button-down collars

00:00:37.478 --> 00:00:40.723
are called button-front
shirts, not button-downs.

00:00:40.723 --> 00:00:43.051
The triangle on the front
of some sweatshirts,

00:00:43.051 --> 00:00:47.027
was originally put there as
extra fabric to absorb sweat.

00:00:47.027 --> 00:00:49.593
The YKK that is on all of your zippers

00:00:49.593 --> 00:00:52.690
stands for Yoshida Kogyo Kabushikikaisha.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.232
And women shirts button on
the opposite side as men's,

00:00:56.232 --> 00:00:58.744
because women used to
be dressed by servants,

00:00:58.744 --> 00:01:02.247
and this way the button would
be in the servants right hand,

00:01:02.247 --> 00:01:05.854
as it is for men dressing themselves.

00:01:05.854 --> 00:01:08.336
One in eight men surveyed
confessed to wearing their

00:01:08.336 --> 00:01:10.871
underwear two to three
times between washes,

00:01:10.871 --> 00:01:12.935
and three of three people we just surveyed

00:01:12.935 --> 00:01:15.348
said, "Eww," after hearing that.

00:01:15.348 --> 00:01:20.348
(lively drums)

